Develop a Verilog module for the following operations. Assume positive clock/clk edge triggering unless otherwise noted.
You have a fourteen-bit input vector in[13:0]. Calculate the following:
// (1) out_and: Each bit of this output vector should indicate the logical AND between the corresponding input bit and its neighbour to the left. For example, out_and[3] should be the AND of in[3] and in[4]. Since in[13] has no neighbour to the left, out_and[13] is not needed.
// (2) out_nor: Each bit of this output vector should indicate the logical NOR between the corresponding input bit and its neighbour to the right. For example, out_nor[10] should be the NOR of in[10] and in[9]. Since in[0] has no neighbour to the right, out_nor[0] is not needed.
// (3) out_xor_wrap: Each bit of this output vector should indicate the XOR between the corresponding input bit and its neighbour to the right. For this part, treat the vector as wrapping around, so in[0]'s neighbour to the right is in[13].

code:
