description:
Design a 32-bit wide binary up-counter that increments its output `q` on each rising edge of the clock signal `clk`. The counter resets to zero when it reaches a predefined value `N` (set to 100). This module can be used for applications requiring counting or timing functionality, such as timers or frequency dividers.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    output reg [31:0] q
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    output reg [31:0] q
);parameter N = 100;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (q == N) begin
        q <= 0;
    end
    else begin
        q <= q + 1;
    end
end

endmodule

