description:
Design a 15-bit Linear Feedback Shift Register (LFSR) that generates a pseudo-random sequence of bits based on a clock signal. The circuit resets when the Reset signal is low, initializing the LFSR with a preset value. On each rising edge of the Clock, the LFSR updates its bits using a feedback mechanism from specific bits (bit 14 and bit 13) while shifting the other bits. Additionally, the module produces a HIGH output (Out) when the LFSR reaches a specific predefined state (15'b001000010001100), effectively functioning as a sequence generator with a detectable output condition.
module top_module(
input Clock,
input Reset,
output reg Out
);

code:
module top_module(
input Clock,
input Reset,
output reg Out
);reg [14:0] LFSR;

always @(posedge Clock, negedge Reset) begin
	if(Reset==0) begin
		Out <= 0;
		LFSR <= 15'b111111111111111;
	end
	else begin
		LFSR[0] <= LFSR[13] ^ LFSR[14];
		LFSR[14:1] <= LFSR[13:0];
		if(LFSR==15'b001000010001100) Out <= 1;
	end
end

endmodule

