description:
Design a simple counter circuit that increments a 10-bit output address on each rising edge of a 65 MHz clock signal (CLOCK_65). When the reset signal (rst_n) is asserted low, the address is reset to zero. The module effectively counts from 0 to 1023 (maximum value for 10 bits) in a continuous loop while providing functionality for a synchronous reset.
module top_module(
					address,
					rst_n,
					CLOCK_65
				);

code:
module top_module(
					address,
					rst_n,
					CLOCK_65
				);output [9:0]	address;

		input rst_n;
		input CLOCK_65;

		reg [9:0]	address = 10'b0;

	always @(posedge CLOCK_65 or negedge rst_n)
		begin
			if(!rst_n)
				address = 10'b0;
			else
				address = address + 1'b1;
		end

endmodule

