description:
Develop a circuit that calculates the parity bit for a given input data word and indicates whether the parity is valid. The module takes an n-bit input data vector and, depending on the specified parity type (even or odd), computes the corresponding parity bit. It outputs the parity bit, and an error signal that asserts when the calculated parity does not match the expected parity for the input data. This circuit is useful in error detection for communication systems, ensuring data integrity.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] d,
  output p, e
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] d,
  output p, e
);parameter n = 8; // number of data bits
parameter parity = "even"; // parity type (even or odd)

reg parity_bit;
wire [n-1:0] ones_count;
wire parity_match;

assign ones_count = {n{1'b0}} + d;
assign parity_match = (parity == "even") ? (ones_count % 2 == 0) : (ones_count % 2 == 1);

always @* begin
  if (parity == "even") begin
    parity_bit = (ones_count % 2 == 0) ? 1'b0 : 1'b1;
  end else begin
    parity_bit = (ones_count % 2 == 1) ? 1'b0 : 1'b1;
  end
end

assign p = parity_bit;
assign e = (parity_match) ? 1'b0 : 1'b1;

endmodule

