description:
Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input (representing a hexadecimal digit) into the corresponding 8-bit output for a seven-segment display. The module maps each possible 4-bit input value (0 through F) to a specific pattern that lights up the appropriate segments of the display to visually represent the hexadecimal character. If the input does not match any defined value, the output will default to a state that turns off all segments.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    output reg [7:0] SevenSegValue
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    output reg [7:0] SevenSegValue
);always @(*)
    begin
        case(A)
            4'h0: SevenSegValue = 8'b11000000;
            4'h1: SevenSegValue = 8'b11111001;
            4'h2: SevenSegValue = 8'b10100100;
            4'h3: SevenSegValue = 8'b10110000;
            4'h4: SevenSegValue = 8'b10011001;
            4'h5: SevenSegValue = 8'b10010010;
            4'h6: SevenSegValue = 8'b10000010;
            4'h7: SevenSegValue = 8'b11111000;
            4'h8: SevenSegValue = 8'b10000000;
            4'h9: SevenSegValue = 8'b10010000;
            4'hA: SevenSegValue = 8'b10001000;
            4'hB: SevenSegValue = 8'b10000011;
            4'hC: SevenSegValue = 8'b10100111;
            4'hD: SevenSegValue = 8'b10000110;
            4'hE: SevenSegValue = 8'b10001110;
            4'hF: SevenSegValue = 8'b10011110;
            default: SevenSegValue = 8'b11111111;              
        endcase
    end

endmodule

