description:
Design a 4-bit binary adder module that takes two 4-bit inputs, A and B, and computes their sum, S. The output utilizes wrapping behavior where the sum is constrained within a 4-bit range, effectively implementing modulo-16 addition. If the raw sum exceeds 15, it wraps around by subtracting 16 before outputting the result. This design ensures that the result S is always represented within the bounds of a 4-bit binary number, addressing overflow scenarios.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [3:0] S
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [3:0] S
);reg [3:0] sum1, sum2;

always @(A, B) begin
    sum1 <= A + B;
end

always @(sum1) begin
    if (sum1 > 15) begin
        sum2 <= sum1 - 16;
    end
    else begin
        sum2 <= sum1;
    end
end

always @(sum2) begin
    S <= sum2;
end

endmodule

