description:
Design a debouncer circuit for a button input, ensuring a stable output state in the presence of switch bounce. The module uses a clock input and generates a single-bit output that indicates the stable state of the button. When the button is pressed, it increments a counter until it reaches a defined threshold, at which point the output is asserted as high. If the button is released, the counter resets, and the output becomes low. This implementation effectively cleans up noisy signals from mechanical button presses.
module top_module(
	input clk,
	input button,
	output reg button_state
    );

