description:
Design a module for an I2C Serial Data Line (SDA) interface that can operate in both read and write modes. When in write mode (ReadorWrite=1), the module outputs signals onto the SDA line based on a multiplexer controlled by the Select signal; it can either send a Start/Stop acknowledgment or shift out data depending on the Select and StartStopAck inputs. In read mode (ReadorWrite=0), the SDA line becomes high-impedance (3-state) for external devices to drive it, allowing data to be read through the ShiftIn output. The design enables communication through the I2C protocol by effectively managing data flow and acknowledging operations.
module top_module(input	ReadorWrite, Select, StartStopAck, ShiftOut,
output ShiftIn, inout SDA);

code:
module top_module(input	ReadorWrite, Select, StartStopAck, ShiftOut,
output ShiftIn, inout SDA);reg MuxOut;

assign SDA = (ReadorWrite)? (1'bz):(MuxOut);
assign ShiftIn = SDA;	


always@(ReadorWrite, Select, StartStopAck, ShiftOut)
	case({ReadorWrite, Select})
	2'b00: MuxOut<= StartStopAck;
	2'b01: MuxOut<= ShiftOut;
	2'b10: MuxOut<=0;
	2'b11: MuxOut<=0;
	default: MuxOut<=0;
	endcase	

endmodule

